From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Research page slowness: cache get_angel_ohlc, was
 fetching fresh every single view

Reported today: Research page (and anywhere using stock-chart) felt
generally slow after the Angel migration. Root cause: get_angel_ohlc
had no caching at all - every chart view, every period switch
(1mo/3mo/1y/5y), every repeated look at the same stock triggered a
fresh call to Angel's historical-data endpoint, which has its own
separate, easy-to-trip rate limit (already fixed to retry with
backoff rather than crash, but a 3-20+ second backoff wait is still
very perceptible as "slow" from the user's side).

Fix: added @ttl_cache(ttl_seconds=900) (same decorator, same 15-minute
TTL already used for the yfinance-based fetch_multi_period screener
cache) to get_angel_ohlc. Daily candle data barely changes intraday
except today's still-forming candle, so a 15-minute cache is a
reasonable tradeoff between freshness and not hammering an
easily-rate-limited endpoint on every click.

get_angel_ltp already had its own separate 60s cache (_price_cache) -
unaffected, still fine as is.

Verified: repeated calls for the same symbol+period hit the cache
(only 1 real API call across 2 identical requests), a different
period correctly triggers a fresh fetch (separate cache key), and a
failure that exhausts all retries is correctly NOT cached - a
transient rate-limit hit won't get "stuck" returning a cached failure
on the next attempt, since ttl_cache only stores successful returns
(the exception propagates before the cache-write line ever runs).
All 17 existing tests still pass.
---
 app/services/angel_feed.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/services/angel_feed.py b/app/services/angel_feed.py
index 75cd5a9..3b0b734 100644
--- a/app/services/angel_feed.py
+++ b/app/services/angel_feed.py
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ from datetime import datetime, timedelta
 import requests
 
 from app.config import settings
+from app.cache import ttl_cache
 
 logger = logging.getLogger("angel_feed")
 
@@ -281,6 +282,7 @@ def _call_candle_data_with_retry(api, params: dict, symbol: str) -> dict:
     )
 
 
+@ttl_cache(ttl_seconds=900)
 def get_angel_ohlc(symbol: str, period: str = "1y") -> list:
     """Daily OHLC candles via Angel One's getCandleData - same output shape
     ({time, open, high, low, close}, Lightweight-Charts-ready) as
